From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:15:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] drm/asahi: g15: drain the flights inside the stamp
 renumbering margin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Renumbering only happens at a publication with nothing in flight. A
client that keeps the GPU busy (no vsync) can keep a flight in the air
through the whole margin, and the TA stamp would then wrap as before.
Inside the margin, publish nothing behind a flight, so the flights drain
and the next publication renumbers while idle (once every ~8.7M renders
with a margin of 100000).

Also clamp a non-zero margin to at least one prefix of renders, so that
the last prefix published outside it cannot cross the wrap, and to at
most half the stamp range, so that it cannot renumber on every
publication.

Found while reviewing the previous commit, with a model of prefixes of
1-8 renders: a fully overlapped client wrapped 199/199 times without
this and 0/199 with it. On a J516C, with the earlier stamp_seed() (see
the previous commit), from g15_stamp_base 500000 renders before the
wrap with a margin of 100000 and the GPU kept busy (286875 publications
behind a flight), the stamps were renumbered at render 400000 and
rendering went on past the wrap point to render 526113.

